# CODEOWNERS.example
#
# WHAT THIS IS: a list of who must review changes to which files.
# HOW TO USE IT: rename this file to CODEOWNERS (no ".example"), replace
# @your-github-username with real GitHub usernames, then turn on
# "Require review from Code Owners" in your branch rules (docs/protect-main.md).
#
# NOTE: it only does something when there is a SECOND person who can review.
# If you work alone, GitHub will not let you approve your own pull request,
# so leave this as .example until you have a reviewer.
#
# Format: <file pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]   Later lines win.

# Everything, by default
*                         @your-github-username

# The safety nets themselves -- changes here deserve a careful second look
/.claude/                 @your-github-username
/guard/                   @your-github-username
/.github/                 @your-github-username

# Database rules and migrations
/supabase/                @your-github-username
